{
  "_comment": [
    "Rates in USD per 1M tokens, keyed by the model name the agent reports.",
    "cached_input applies to the cached_input_tokens share of input_tokens.",
    "cache_creation_5m / cache_creation_1h are Claude's prompt cache write rates;",
    "cache_creation is OpenAI's (GPT-5.6 and later, at the default 30-minute TTL).",
    "Keys resolve by exact match, then longest prefix match, then default.",
    "Keys are version-qualified on purpose. A family-wide key such as 'claude-haiku'",
    "prefix-matches every generation, so it keeps applying one generation's rates",
    "after the next one is priced differently -- silently, and reported as though a",
    "rate had matched. A model absent from the table falls to `default` and is",
    "flagged `pricing_matched=false` instead, which is a visible signal.",
    "For the same reason a prefix match may not end inside a version number:",
    "'gpt-5' matches 'gpt-5-2025-08-07' but not 'gpt-5.5', and 'claude-opus-5'",
    "does not match 'claude-opus-5-5'.",
    "long_context replaces the rates for a whole request whose input_tokens exceed",
    "above_input_tokens (OpenAI's >272K tier, Claude Haiku 5.5's >100K tier); the",
    "threshold is checked per request, counting cache reads and writes.",
    "fast replaces them for a Claude request served in fast mode (usage.speed 'fast', or a",
    "'-fast' model id); a fast request on a model without it reports pricing_matched=false.",
    "Rates change: in production, point CAT_OTEL_PRICING_FILE at your own table."
  ],
